     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"With no defences an attack path exists: phish_workstation, then pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc, auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and finally exfiltrate_db. So zero controls is not enough. Deploying mfa:admin alone stops every path. Exfiltration needs admin on the db, fileserver or backup host. Each of those needs a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, and all three need stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs. These need admin_dc or admin_adfs, which need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. Those footholds come only from auth_dc and auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. With mfa:admin deployed, stolen_dbadmin can never be obtained, so exfiltration is impossible. The minimum is 1.\"}"
    }
   ],
